    <td height=3D"21" width=3D"50">
    </td>
    <td height=3D"21" width=3D"100">
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td height=3D"21">
      <i>Step 2</i><font face=3D"Calibri">:
      The dataset is then split on the different attributes. The entropy fo=
r each branch is calculated. Then it is added proportionally, to get total =
entropy for the
      split. The resulting entropy is subtracted from the entropy before th=
e split.
      The result is the Information Gain, or decrease in entropy.&nbsp;</fo=
nt></td>
    <td height=3D"21" width=3D"50">
    </td>
    <td height=3D"21" width=3D"100">
    </td>
  </tr>
